FROM qwen2.5-coder:7b

# Sizing this window from measurements, not from a guess.
#
# The earlier comment here claimed "roughly 15k tokens" for CHAI's prompts. That
# was never measured and is about 2x high for the fixed part.
#
# Measured fixed prompt material (chars), per benchmark, after scoping the
# added-operator few-shot examples to the operators the gatekeeper leaves
# feasible for that app:
#
#     before scoping   27,341  (every app, all ten examples)
#     ar-iclib         21,753     sobel-iclib   22,561
#     stringsearch     22,809     fft-iclib     20,668
#     lqi-iclib        21,533     bc-iclib      20,759
#
# That is ~5.9-6.5K tokens at 3.5 chars/token, plus the benchmark source
# (546-3,173 tokens) and the code-base summary.
#
# The part that actually needs headroom is parent conversation history. Each
# parent function used to contribute its full purpose + plan + generated C +
# the same C again inside the JSON conversion; on a nine-function application
# that is eighteen copies of function bodies. utils/context.py now summarises
# each parent to its purpose, signature, and knobs, and the JSON conversion
# round trip is gone entirely when a structured plan is available.
#
# utils/token_budget.py records the real per-function context size to
# logs/context_budget_<app>_<profile>.json on every run. Resize this window
# from those files. Do not shrink it on the basis of this comment alone:
# an undersized num_ctx truncates silently.
#
# The stock Ollama runtime defaults to 4k, which discards most of the prompt.
PARAMETER num_ctx 24576
PARAMETER num_predict 2048
PARAMETER temperature 0
